# AGENTS.md: Working agreement

This repo is built to be handed between agents (and humans). Follow this and a
fresh agent can pick up any unit of work without prior context. If a rule here
conflicts with a request, surface the conflict rather than silently overriding it.

## Commands

The full gate, the same one CI runs. Run it before every commit:

```sh
{{CHECK_CMD}}
```

## The loop (every session)

1. Read `STATUS.md` (it is short) and the current phase in `ROADMAP.md`. For what
   happened recently, run `git log --oneline -15`.
2. Pick one unit of work whose dependencies are done. Read its plan/phase doc fully.
3. Work on a branch (`feat/<short-slug>` or `phase-N/<short-slug>`).
4. Before stopping, fix any line of `STATUS.md` that is no longer true. If
   nothing in it changed, leave it alone. What you did goes in the commit body.

## Non-negotiables (Definition of Done)

Copy-pasteable into a PR description; the PR template mirrors this list.

- [ ] The gate is green locally: `{{CHECK_CMD}}`.
- [ ] New behavior has tests; every bug fix has a regression test that fails
      against the broken code.
- [ ] `STATUS.md` is still true. Edit it only if this change made a line false.
- [ ] No secrets, no committed data, no `{{PROJECT_SLUG}}`-external paths.
      Secrets live in `.env` (git-ignored), listed by name in `.env.example`;
      never print, log, or commit a key value.

## STATUS.md is a snapshot, not a log

It says where things stand now, in four short sections, and has a hard limit of
60 lines that `scripts/check-docs.sh` enforces. Never add a dated entry, a list
of finished work, or a changelog to it or to any other file: history is
`git log`. If the check fails, delete what is stale. Do not move it elsewhere,
and do not raise the limit; that is the owner's decision.

